# SYNTHETIC. Written from RFC 5321 and RFC 4954. Not a recording:
# phase-0 capture against a real server has not happened yet.
# Full submission. The greeting and EHLO are multi-line. AUTH PLAIN carries
# the initial response. The body line that begins with '.' is sent stuffed.

S: 220-smtp.example ESMTP
S: 220 ready
C: EHLO client.example
S: 250-smtp.example Hello
S: 250-SIZE 35882577
S: 250-8BITMIME
S: 250-AUTH PLAIN LOGIN XOAUTH2
S: 250 PIPELINING
C: AUTH PLAIN AGFkYUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbQBzM2NyM3QtcGFzc3dvcmQ=
S: 235 2.7.0 Authentication successful
C: MAIL FROM:<ada@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.0 OK
C: RCPT TO:<bob@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.5 OK
C: RCPT TO:<cara@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.5 OK
C: DATA
S: 354 End data with <CR><LF>.<CR><LF>
C: From: ada@example.com
C: To: bob@example.com
C: Subject: hello
C:
C: Hi.
C: ..this starts with a dot
C: Bye
C: .
S: 250 2.0.0 OK queued
C: QUIT
S: 221 2.0.0 Bye
DONE
